From f079e0abd33e7d11d5f59b031bed5630aeeafc68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ERICA Sentry <root@amd-ecp>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] spi: cadence-quadspi: bound periodic-tuning wait (6.18) to
 fix resume AB-BA deadlock

Adapts the 2025.2 (kernel 6.12) fix to the 2026.1 kernel (6.18,
xlnx_rebase_v6.18_LTS_2026.1), whose per-CS DLL-tuning rework restructured
cqspi_periodictuning() but kept the same unbounded-wait / cancel hazard.

An intermittent hang on deep-suspend resume (PSCI SYSTEM_SUSPEND) on Versal
Gen 2 / VEK385 is a classic AB-BA deadlock between two D-state tasks:

  (A) the resume/exec thread
      ... -> spi_nor_resume -> spi_nor_init -> spi_nor_read_id
          -> spi_mem_exec_op -> cqspi_exec_mem_op
              refcount_inc(&cqspi->inflight_ops);
          -> cqspi_setup_phymode()
          -> cancel_delayed_work_sync(&mem->complete_work)
          -> wait_for_completion()        [waits for the tuning work to end]

  (B) the periodic-tuning work item
      cqspi_periodictuning()
          -> wait_for_completion(&mem->request_completion)
                                          [waits for an in-flight mem op]

(A) holds an in-flight OSPI mem op (request_completion not yet signalled)
and waits to cancel the tuning work; (B) is that tuning work, parked forever
on request_completion.  Neither can progress -> resume (and every async
device resumer waiting on the QSPI parent) wedges.

6.18 added an 'if (refcount_read(&cqspi->inflight_ops) > 1) reschedule'
early-bail at the top of cqspi_periodictuning(), but that is a check-then-act
guard: cqspi_exec_mem_op() only increments inflight_ops AFTER the periodic
work may have already passed the guard, so the work can still enter the
unbounded wait_for_completion(&mem->request_completion) while the exec path
runs cancel_delayed_work_sync().  The window is small but is exactly the
resume path that re-runs the setup/tuning code.

Bound that wait with wait_for_completion_timeout(CQSPI_TUNING_TIMEOUT_MS).
On timeout the work reschedules instead of holding off the
cancel_delayed_work_sync() in the exec/resume path, so (A) is released
(after at most CQSPI_TUNING_TIMEOUT_MS in the worst racing case) and the
resume completes.  The existing '!request_completion.done' guard is
preserved so an already-signalled completion is not consumed.  Both
CQSPI_TUNING_TIMEOUT_MS and CQSPI_TUNING_PERIODICITY_MS are already defined
and used in this driver.

Signed-off-by: ERICA Sentry <root@amd-ecp>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-cadence-quadspi.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-cadence-quadspi.c b/drivers/spi/spi-cadence-quadspi.c
index 39f7834..8893c2a 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-cadence-quadspi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-cadence-quadspi.c
@@ -975,11 +975,29 @@ static void cqspi_periodictuning(struct work_struct *work)
 	}
 
 	/*
-	 * Wait for any ongoing flash operation to complete before tuning.
-	 * The request_completion is signaled when the flash is idle.
+	 * Wait (BOUNDED) for any ongoing flash operation to complete before
+	 * tuning.  An unbounded wait_for_completion() here can AB-BA deadlock
+	 * against the exec/resume path: cqspi_exec_mem_op() increments
+	 * inflight_ops and then cqspi_setup_phymode() calls
+	 * cancel_delayed_work_sync(&mem->complete_work), which waits for THIS
+	 * work to return, while this work waits on request_completion.  The
+	 * inflight_ops > 1 guard above only NARROWS the window: it is a
+	 * check-then-act race, so an op can go in-flight (and take the
+	 * cancel_delayed_work_sync path) after the guard passes but before this
+	 * wait.  It is hit on deep-suspend resume, where the setup path re-runs
+	 * to re-establish the DLL tuning.  Bound the wait so the work bails out
+	 * and reschedules instead of wedging the whole resume.  The existing
+	 * !done guard is preserved so an already-signalled completion is not
+	 * consumed.
 	 */
-	if (!mem->request_completion.done)
-		wait_for_completion(&mem->request_completion);
+	if (!mem->request_completion.done &&
+	    !wait_for_completion_timeout(&mem->request_completion,
+					 msecs_to_jiffies(CQSPI_TUNING_TIMEOUT_MS))) {
+		/* Op still in flight; skip this cycle and retry later. */
+		schedule_delayed_work(&mem->complete_work,
+				      msecs_to_jiffies(CQSPI_TUNING_PERIODICITY_MS));
+		return;
+	}
 
 	/*
 	 * Block new operations during tuning by reinit'ing tuning_complete.
